export function classroomGuide(staff){return '<section class="vle-panel"><h2>Classroom quick start</h2><p>'+(staff?'Plan, teach, mark and follow up from one workspace.':'Find your next task, hand in work and read your feedback.')+'</p><div class="vle-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="#/classroom?view=today">Open Today</a><a class="btn" href="#/classroom?view=classes">Open my classrooms</a></div></section><div class="vle-grid">'+(staff?'<section class="vle-panel"><h3>Set work</h3><ol><li>Open a classroom and choose <strong>Units</strong>, <strong>Classwork</strong> or <strong>Materials</strong>.</li><li>Create an assignment or quiz. The <strong>Additional</strong> menu contains extra activities. Save a draft to finish later.</li><li>Use the collapsed Options for objectives, release dates, individual deadlines and selected students. Publish when ready.</li><li>Use Stream for announcements. Pin important messages, or archive old ones and restore them later.</li></ol></section><section class="vle-panel"><h3>Mark and report</h3><ol><li><a href="#/classroom?view=inbox">To mark</a> brings together submissions from your classes.</li><li>Save a private marking draft, or return marks and feedback to the student.</li><li><strong>Add scores to MIS</strong> opens a preview. Choose the returned scores to transfer; returning feedback alone does not update the MIS.</li><li>Use Progress for units and objectives, or Materials → Class reading overview for reading confirmations.</li></ol></section><section class="vle-panel"><h3>Reuse and support</h3><p>Save assessments or questions to Library, copy a unit to another allocated class, and review its draft tasks and dates before publishing.</p><p>Private help stays between a pupil and their allocated teacher. Discussion replies can require moderation. Portfolio entries reach linked families only after teacher approval and explicit sharing.</p></section>':'<section class="vle-panel"><h3>Work through your day</h3><ol><li><a href="#/classroom?view=today">Today</a> shows what to do next. Week shows deadlines, lessons and class events.</li><li>Open a task, read the instructions and save your answers. Wait for the saved message before leaving.</li><li><strong>Turn in</strong> hands work to your teacher. Saving a draft does not hand it in.</li><li>Use Ask for help on a task when you are stuck.</li></ol></section><section class="vle-panel"><h3>Read and improve</h3><ol><li><a href="#/classroom?view=reading">My reading</a> lists guides from all your subjects.</li><li>Open a guide, read it, then choose <strong>I’ve read this</strong>. Updated guides need a new confirmation.</li><li>Read returned feedback and acknowledge it. You can reflect on changes and resubmit when needed.</li><li>My progress shows returned results and your learning path. Portfolio lets you collect evidence for teacher review.</li></ol></section>')+'<section class="vle-panel"><h3>Testing this demo</h3><p>Use fictional information. Changes are saved in this browser and are not shared with colleagues or other devices.</p><p>To test a full hand-in and marking cycle, sign out and switch between the student and teacher test accounts in this same browser. The login page lists the accounts.</p><p>The free demo does not send email, connect external accounts, provide live document co-editing or synchronise devices.</p></section></div>';}
